pokeplatinum-widepointers2.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it to build/pokeplatinum, after widepointers): the pointer
pass's rule for locals. A u32 local that takes a pointer through a (uintptr_t) cast (widepointers' casts) is a uintptr_t:
pret's C keeps the address in it, adds to it or aligns it, and turns it back into a pointer (particle_system.c's
ParticleSystem_AllocMemory cut the heap address, and the opening's SPLManager_New wrote through it). Every such local, as
a rule: a widening of the local only.

